(Stage 1d — `a value called "r"` locals. Codegen and the analyzer already
 handled Type::Value declarations; only the parser never accepted the noun
 in a declaration position, so the documented syntax did not compile. A
 local carries its tag through printing, predicates, reassignment, and an
 append back into a list.)

To echo with a value called v. Return a value, v.

a value called first_slot is echo of "hello".
print first_slot.
If first_slot is a text, print "text".
Otherwise print "not text".

set first_slot to 7.
print first_slot.
If first_slot is a number, print "number now".
Otherwise print "still text".

a value called second_slot is echo of 3.5.
a list called out is [].
append first_slot to out.
append second_slot to out.
print out.
